        "title": "Emergency Visit \u2014 Traumatic Tooth Avulsion",
        "section": [
          {
            "title": "Subjective",
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns='http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml'>21-year-old presents after being struck in the mouth during a basketball game ~40 minutes prior. Tooth #9 completely avulsed, kept in milk during transport. Pain 7/10.</div>"
            }
          },
          {
            "title": "Objective",
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns='http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml'>Tooth #9 avulsed with intact root, minimal extraoral dry time. Socket irrigated, tooth re-implanted and splinted with flexible wire-composite splint. PA radiograph confirms good alignment, no root fracture.</div>"
            }
          },
          {
            "title": "Assessment",
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns='http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml'>Traumatic avulsion of permanent maxillary central incisor, successfully replanted.</div>"
            }
          },
          {
            "title": "Plan",
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns='http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml'>Amoxicillin and ibuprofen prescribed. Splint to remain 2 weeks. Follow-up in 1-2 weeks for splint removal and pulp vitality check, then again at 4 weeks \u2014 critical to monitor for resorption/ankylosis.</div>"
            }
          }
        ]
      },
